## 6. Decisions

**D1 — Does the blue panel scroll, or must everything always fit?**
Recommended: **always fit down to 320×568**, with scrolling only as the safety net for
screens that genuinely cannot (the stock grid, which is already a scroller). A keypad you
have to scroll is a broken keypad.

**D2 — Dock on feature screens: collapse, or hide?**
Recommended: **collapse** (§3.2) — navigation stays reachable and the layout height stays
constant between screens. Hiding is defensible since every feature screen has its own ✕ / ✓,
and it would give back another 64px. Your call.

> **New evidence, 2026-08-17.** The authoritative phone design
> `docs/designs/motion-tablet-desktop/uploads/retail terminal.png` — surfaced during review
> of the companion plan — shows the retail terminal **home** screen with **no dock at all**,
> and an active stack of three rows in the space the dock currently occupies. That is a
> point for "hide", and it raises a question this decision did not previously contemplate:
> whether the dock belongs on the terminal *home* screen either. Settle D2 against the
> design, not against the arithmetic.

**D3 — Fallback if the goo misbehaves on iOS.**
A geometry-only morph: one element animating `width`/`height`/`border-radius` from pill to
handle with a squash-and-stretch overshoot, icons fading first. Reads as melting rather than
oozing — no meniscus, no surface tension — but it is bulletproof and cheap. Recommend
building the choreography so the goo layer is a *enhancement* that can be switched off by a
single flag, rather than the mechanism the timing depends on.

**D4 — Swipe distance and direction.**
Recommended: **56px of upward travel or a 0.4px/ms flick**, with the dock tracking the
finger throughout, and a downward swipe collapsing it again. Worth feeling on a real device
before fixing the numbers.

