## 7. Execution order

| Phase | Content | Gate |
|---|---|---|
| A | `--dock-h` measured and published by `TerminalDockView`; every screen consumes it | no content behind the dock on any of 5 screens × 6 sizes |
| B | `.tp-screen` grid + `min-height: 0` + `.tp-panel-body` scroll region; delete the six hand-tuned paddings | nothing clipped past the viewport; hero yields before the panel does |
| C | Fluid keypad/tile sizing via the companion plan's tokens | 4 keypad rows visible without scrolling at 320×568 |
| D | Dock `collapsed` control prop; terminal collapses it on feature screens | `--dock-h` reports 64 on a feature screen, 78 on home |
| E | Pointer-tracked swipe: shrink the hit area, drop `onTouchStart`/`onMouseMove`, add the `aria-expanded` keyboard path | a tap anywhere on the strip does **not** expand; a 56px upward drag does; Enter on the handle does; page scroll near the bottom edge still works |
| F | Two-layer goo morph, filter only during transition, reduced-motion path | icons legible at every frame; `filter: none` at rest in both states; no dropped frames on device |

**Sequencing constraints.** B depends on A, and on the companion plan's Phase 2 token layer.
C depends on B. F depends on D and E (the morph is only worth building once the collapsed
state is a state you enter deliberately). A, D and E are independently shippable.

**Do not break:** the `TerminalDockView` purity boundary test; the landing demo's
`placement="absolute" collapseAfterMs={null}` mount; the tablet/desktop app, which uses its
own chrome and must not see any of this.
